  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets where shadows bite.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold, devoid of cheer.\n\nLike ghosts, the crowds drifted by,\nWith eyes cast down, no glance would fly.\nLost in their own deep, private spheres,\nHe vanished in the urban seas.\n\nAmidst the tide of faceless men,\nA profound solitude began,\nTo wrap him tight in silent night,\nAlone beneath the streetlamp’s light.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
